{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) issued stitch task #5559 to implement `cmd/mkfifo` - a Go reimplementation of GNU mkfifo that creates named pipes (FIFOs). The task covers SRD092 requirements R1.1 through R1.4: creating FIFOs via mkfifo(2), handling multiple arguments, supporting `-m MODE`/`--mode=MODE` for permission bits (octal or symbolic, default 0666 modified by umask), and proper error handling with exit code 1 on failure while continuing to process remaining arguments. Two files must be created: `cmd/mkfifo/main.go` and `cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Named pipe (FIFO) creation using `syscall.Mkfifo()` system call\n   - Permission mode parsing (octal like `0644` and symbolic like `a=rw`)\n   - Differential testing against `gmkfifo` (Homebrew GNU coreutils reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` / `testutils.BuildBinary` / `testutils.DiffTest` struct for test harness\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gmkfifo\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for differential tests\n   - Continue processing remaining args on error, track overall failure status\n   - Default FIFO mode: 0666 modified by umask\n   - 40-line function size limit, 500-line file size limit\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd092-mkfifo.yaml` (read)\n     - Full SRD for mkfifo with requirements R1 (FIFO creation) and R2 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - R1.1: Create FIFO at each path using mkfifo(2)\n     - R1.2: Process multiple NAME arguments\n     - R1.3: `-m MODE` / `--mode=MODE` sets permission bits (octal or symbolic), default 0666 modified by umask\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 on failure, print error to stderr, continue processing remaining args\n     - R2.1: Exit 0 on all success; R2.2: Exit 1 on any failure; R2.3: SIGPIPE handler\n     - Non-goals: No SELinux context setting\n     - Package imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (read)\n     - Confirms SIGPIPE handler pattern used across all cmd/ utilities\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (from package_contracts, not read directly)\n     - DiffTest struct: `type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package\n\n   - `cmd/chmod/mode.go` exists in repository (listed in files) but NOT read - contains symbolic mode parsing that could be referenced for R1.3's symbolic mode support\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that mkfifo is a filesystem-mutating utility (creates FIFOs), so differential tests need to run in temp directories and compare exit codes + stderr output rather than just stdout\n   - Determined the need for both octal and symbolic mode parsing per R1.3\n   - Noted that `cmd/chmod/mode.go` exists and may have reusable mode parsing logic, but per constraints should implement from scratch following go_style_constitution\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with extensive project context, SRD references, execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, requirements, design decisions, and acceptance criteria for implementing cmd/mkfifo (R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting this summary\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/mkfifo/main.go` with FIFO creation, multiple argument handling, `-m`/`--mode` flag for permission bits, and error handling\n   - Create `cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go` with differential tests against `gmkfifo`\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/mkfifo/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/mkfifo/` to verify no warnings (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/mkfifo/ -count=1` to verify differential tests pass (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (srd092-mkfifo.yaml and pkg/sys/sigpipe.go) and was about to write the implementation. The task requires creating two files:\n   \n   **cmd/mkfifo/main.go** needs to:\n   - Start with copyright header\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Parse `-m`/`--mode` flag (default \"0666\")\n   - Parse mode string (octal like \"0755\" or symbolic like \"a=rw\")\n   - Iterate over remaining args, calling `syscall.Mkfifo(path, mode)` for each\n   - On error: print to stderr in GNU format (`mkfifo: cannot create fifo 'NAME': reason`), set failure flag, continue\n   - Exit 0 if all succeed, exit 1 if any fail\n   - Print usage error if no NAME arguments provided\n\n   **cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go** needs to:\n   - Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gmkfifo\")`\n   - Skip if gmkfifo not found\n   - Define `[]testutils.DiffTest` test cases covering: single FIFO creation, multiple FIFOs, mode setting with `-m`, error on existing path, missing arguments\n   - Use temp directories via WorkDir for filesystem operations\n   - Call `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/mkfifo/main.go` and `cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go` in full, then run build and test verification. The task description states: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands\" and the implementation strategy says to \"write each file in dependency order, then compile and test once.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5559/68a401e8-7e6a-4f21-8430-ea931fdf1c0c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68a401e8-7e6a-4f21-8430-ea931fdf1c0c","uuid":"455a274e-af11-4132-b743-5b4385c35ac0","timestamp":"2026-05-24T02:06:12.669Z","isSynthetic":true}
