{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JSyUW6WkNJXbPcMWmeK5EY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have what you need. Here's the key information:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe test framework handles filesystem-creating commands like `touch`, `mkdir`, etc. through the `DiffTest` structure and its workdir management.\n\n### How WorkDir is Handled (from `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5559/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`):\n\n**Lines 92-105** show the critical logic:\n\n```go\nfunc runSubtest(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tc DiffTest) {\n    t.Helper()\n    workDir := tc.WorkDir\n    if workDir == \"\" {\n        workDir = t.TempDir()  // Create fresh temp dir if not specified\n    }\n    env := buildEnv(tc.Env)\n    goRes := runBinary(t, goBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n    refRes := runBinary(t, refBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n    // ... normalizers and comparison\n    checkExpectedFiles(t, workDir, tc.ExpectedFiles)\n}\n```\n\n**Critical cleanup strategy:**\n1. **Same WorkDir for both**: Both the Go binary and reference binary run in the SAME `workDir` (lines 99-100)\n2. **Sequential execution**: Go binary runs first, then reference binary—both in same directory\n3. **File validation happens after both**: `checkExpectedFiles()` at line 104 verifies files exist and match expected content\n\n### The touch_test.go Example (showing real usage):\n\n**Lines 209-231** show how they handle this for tests that need pre-existing files:\n\n```go\nrefDir1 := t.TempDir()\nos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(refDir1, \"existing\"), []byte{}, 0644)\nrefDir2 := t.TempDir()\nos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(refDir2, \"existing\"), []byte{}, 0644)\n\ntests = append(tests,\n    testutils.DiffTest{\n        Name:    \"reference file short flag\",\n        Args:    []string{\"-r\", \"existing\", \"rfile\"},\n        WorkDir: refDir1,  // EXPLICIT separate temp dir per test\n        ExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n            \"rfile\": {},\n        },\n    },\n    // ...\n)\n```\n\n### The Pattern:\n\n- **For tests needing clean separation**: Create separate `t.TempDir()` instances and pass via `WorkDir` field\n- **For tests that don't create conflicting files**: Reuse the same `workDir` (both binaries run in it sequentially—no cleanup needed between them because they're not creating conflicting artifacts)\n- **File verification**: The `ExpectedFiles` map validates filesystem state after both binaries complete\n\nThe framework doesn't do inter-run cleanup—it relies on running both binaries in the same directory sequentially, then validating the final state matches expectations."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68a401e8-7e6a-4f21-8430-ea931fdf1c0c","uuid":"5ee64b7c-4646-4fd6-bf93-cd75f963a595","timestamp":"2026-05-24T02:06:52.625Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5559, find an example of a cmd/ test that creates files in the filesystem (not just comparing stdout). Look at cmd/mkdir or cmd/touch or cmd/mknod tests - any utility that creates filesystem artifacts. I need to understand how they handle WorkDir in DiffTest and clean up between the go binary and reference binary runs. Show me the test file content. Quick search.","agentId":"a0a1b6ddf498a54e0","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have what you need. Here's the key information:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe test framework handles filesystem-creating commands like `touch`, `mkdir`, etc. through the `DiffTest` structure and its workdir management.\n\n### How WorkDir is Handled (from `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5559/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`):\n\n**Lines 92-105** show the critical logic:\n\n```go\nfunc runSubtest(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tc DiffTest) {\n    t.Helper()\n    workDir := tc.WorkDir\n    if workDir == \"\" {\n        workDir = t.TempDir()  // Create fresh temp dir if not specified\n    }\n    env := buildEnv(tc.Env)\n    goRes := runBinary(t, goBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n    refRes := runBinary(t, refBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n    // ... normalizers and comparison\n    checkExpectedFiles(t, workDir, tc.ExpectedFiles)\n}\n```\n\n**Critical cleanup strategy:**\n1. **Same WorkDir for both**: Both the Go binary and reference binary run in the SAME `workDir` (lines 99-100)\n2. **Sequential execution**: Go binary runs first, then reference binary—both in same directory\n3. **File validation happens after both**: `checkExpectedFiles()` at line 104 verifies files exist and match expected content\n\n### The touch_test.go Example (showing real usage):\n\n**Lines 209-231** show how they handle this for tests that need pre-existing files:\n\n```go\nrefDir1 := t.TempDir()\nos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(refDir1, \"existing\"), []byte{}, 0644)\nrefDir2 := t.TempDir()\nos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(refDir2, \"existing\"), []byte{}, 0644)\n\ntests = append(tests,\n    testutils.DiffTest{\n        Name:    \"reference file short flag\",\n        Args:    []string{\"-r\", \"existing\", \"rfile\"},\n        WorkDir: refDir1,  // EXPLICIT separate temp dir per test\n        ExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n            \"rfile\": {},\n        },\n    },\n    // ...\n)\n```\n\n### The Pattern:\n\n- **For tests needing clean separation**: Create separate `t.TempDir()` instances and pass via `WorkDir` field\n- **For tests that don't create conflicting files**: Reuse the same `workDir` (both binaries run in it sequentially—no cleanup needed between them because they're not creating conflicting artifacts)\n- **File verification**: The `ExpectedFiles` map validates filesystem state after both binaries complete\n\nThe framework doesn't do inter-run cleanup—it relies on running both binaries in the same directory sequentially, then validating the final state matches expectations."}],"totalDurationMs":23373,"totalTokens":29066,"totalToolUseCount":7,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3063,"cache_read_input_tokens":25254,"output_tokens":744,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3063},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":744,"cache_read_input_tokens":25254,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3063,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
