{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AWEvxntZ2c3WGC3kfeFL7v","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide a comprehensive analysis.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully examined the test files. Here are my findings:\n\n### Files Found\n1. **mkdir_test.go** - EXISTS at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5559/cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go`\n2. **mknod_test.go** - DOES NOT EXIST (mknod command doesn't exist in this repo)\n3. **touch_test.go** - EXISTS at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5559/cmd/touch/touch_test.go`\n\n### How They Handle the Directory-Already-Exists Problem\n\nBoth mkdir and touch use a **clever strategy**: they create **separate temporary directories** for each binary rather than trying to run both in the same WorkDir. Looking at the test patterns:\n\n**mkdir_test.go approach:**\n- Lines 86-100: In `runCreationTest()`, separate `TempDir()` calls create independent directories for the Go and reference binaries (lines 371-372)\n- Lines 111-119, 121-130, 148-157: When tests need a pre-existing condition, the test creates the condition independently in each binary's directory before running them\n\n**touch_test.go approach:**\n- Lines 209-230: Creates separate reference directories (`refDir1` and `refDir2`) for specific tests that need pre-existing files\n- Lines 235-508: Regular tests use the default behavior where each binary gets its own temp directory (handled by `RunDiffTests` in testutils)\n\n### How They Handle Binary Name Differences in stderr\n\nBoth use **regex-based normalization functions** that standardize output before comparison:\n\n**mkdir_test.go (lines 431-435):**\n```go\nvar binaryNameRe = regexp.MustCompile(`(/\\S+/)?g?mkdir\\b`)\n\nfunc normalizeBinaryName(b []byte) []byte {\n\treturn binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"mkdir\"))\n}\n```\